# Trivy allowlist for amorae-web container scans. One CVE ID per line;
# # for comments. HIGH+CRITICAL fail CI unless listed here with a
# justification.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# starlette 0.46.2 — transitive via fastapi==0.115.12 (pins starlette<0.47).
# All three fixes require starlette 1.x, i.e. leaving the FastAPI 0.115 line
# for 0.141 — a major web-framework bump with real regression risk, tracked
# as its own PR (see DAILY-LOG 2026-08-09). Each is accepted below with a
# reason specific to THIS deployment, not a blanket "transitive dep" wave.
# Keep this in sync with pip-audit-ignore.txt — same dependency, same story.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# CVE-2026-54283 — request.form() ignores max_fields/max_part_size for
# application/x-www-form-urlencoded (unauthenticated DoS). This one was
# genuinely reachable: every form endpoint here is unauthenticated and the
# age gate is the public entry point. MITIGATED in app code by the
# LimitRequestBody middleware (256 KB request-body cap), which bounds both
# the many-fields and huge-field vectors before the parser runs — verified
# by tests/test_security_headers.py. Suppressed because mitigated, not
# because unreachable.
CVE-2026-54283

# CVE-2026-48818 — SSRF / NTLM credential theft via UNC paths in StaticFiles.
# Windows-only (UNC \\host\share semantics). amorae runs Linux containers on
# the swarm, so this is not applicable here — suppressed on platform, not on
# risk appetite.
CVE-2026-48818

# CVE-2025-62727 — DoS via Range-header merging on file responses. Reachable
# surface is StaticFiles, which here serves only small assets (feed.js ~9 KB,
# css, a handful of SVGs, a 27 KB jpg); the feed's real video is served by the
# CDN, never by this app, and static is Cloudflare-cached. Low impact until
# the starlette upgrade lands.
CVE-2025-62727
